{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"be50cb49-00b8-4b13-84b4-a170f62417e3","status":"SUCCESS","response":"## Observed Baseline Result\n\nThe `inspect` output reveals the **deliberate defect** in [`checkout.py`](file:///Users/xxxxx/Repository/session-bench/artifacts/v1-expanded-preparation/live-captures/antigravity-2026-10-05-02/workspace/fixture_project/checkout.py):\n\n```python\n# Deliberate R1 defect: quantity is ignored and delivery is always charged.\nsubtotal = sum(price for price, quantity in items)  # quantity is never used!\nreturn subtotal + 5\n```\n\nThe `baseline` run confirms **2 of 3 tests fail**:\n\n| Items | Expected | Actual | Pass? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `[(10, 2), (5, 1)]` | `(10×2 + 5×1) + 5 = 30` | `(10 + 5) + 5 = 20` | ❌ |\n| `[(25, 2)]` | `(25×2) + 5 = 55`… wait, expected=50 → `25×2 + 0? No`: `25×2=50` + 5=55… actual=30 → `25+5=30` | `25 + 5 = 30` | ❌ |\n| `[(49, 1)]` | `(49×1) + 5 = 54` | `49 + 5 = 54` | ✅ (quantity=1, so defect is invisible) |\n\n**Root cause:** The generator expression `sum(price for price, quantity in items)` unpacks each tuple correctly but **silently discards `quantity`**, summing only the unit prices. The fix required by R1 is to multiply: `sum(price * quantity for price, quantity in items)`. The third test passes by coincidence because `quantity=1`, making `price×1 == price`.\n\nSB_SURVIVAL_V1_RESPONSE_R1_cafe_🙂\n","duration_seconds":19.094334,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":7121,"output_tokens":937,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":38865,"total_tokens":8058}}}
